flowchart TB
  accTitle: Portable Rust boundary to test
  accDescr: Rust owns versioned cryptographic operations and membership validation. Swift and Kotlin adapters own platform integration. Replication ownership is an explicit decision; storage and crypto are not automatically the same component.
  Mac["💻 Native Mac<br/>SwiftUI / AppKit"] --> Swift["Swift native facade"]
  Expo["📱 Expo UI<br/>TypeScript"] --> Module["Expo native module<br/>Swift / Kotlin"]
  Swift --> FFI["UniFFI candidate<br/>coarse calls + structured errors"]
  Module --> FFI
  subgraph rust["🦀 Proposed portable Rust library — no implementation yet"]
    FFI --> Protocol["Vault protocol<br/>versions + membership validation"]
    Protocol --> Primitives["Vetted crypto dependencies<br/>envelopes + record AEAD"]
    Protocol --> Result["Validated transition result<br/>no hidden network or DB writes"]
  end
  Keystore["🔑 Native key storage per device<br/>lock / restore behavior"] --- Swift
  Keystore --- Module
  Result --> Replica["Replica / domain engine<br/>Rust or conformance-tested adapters<br/>R07 decision before freezing API"]
  Replica --> Store["Platform transaction boundary<br/>records + outbox + checkpoints"]
  Store --> Transport["Relay transport<br/>retries stored ciphertext"]
  JS["JS receives UI data / opaque handles<br/>not long-lived vault keys"] -.-> Module
